(A `value` holds its own copy of what is stored in it, so a list parameter
 given a `value` holding a list receives a copy: the append stays in the
 function's list.)
a value called box is ["a", "b"].
To 'add to' with a list called items.
    append "c" to items.
    Print "items: {items}".

'add to' of box.
Print "box: {box}".
